{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"850780876140183553","content":"When I made Arbiter guns, I set out for one major design concept, making them unique from bows and crossbows (rather than just reskinns, or just upgrades).  So in tier one, average combat is 3 rounds and tier 2 average combat is 5 (base game)\n\nSo any weapon that can be used 5 times or more, generally wont need reloading unless someone gets extra attacks.  Most players frontload damage, so if they have an option of a little for 5 rounds, or a lot of 2 or 3, they will pick the two or three.\n\nSo what i did was say, guns take 1 minute to reload (thus effectively cant be reloaded in combat).  Being someone that regularly shoots guns, 1 minute is a fair reload time.  Then if damage is better than a longbow, it needs to have a cost.\n\nLook at the gun I designed for this season, The base damage is the revolver damage (casue I didnt want it to be a step back compared to other firearm base damages), along with it burning spells slots.  Damage is based on DMG custom spell damage (tho instead of aoes having ~2d6 per level, i did 1d10 which is the single target damage or healing).\n\nSo overall its a single cone shot, with just slightly better than bow damage so its on par with the firearms we use, uses an attunement slot, and for the cost of aspell slot does damage roughtly on par with spells you would use at those levels (lvl 1 and 2 slots are better, lvl 3 is abotu the same, and everything else is a bit less)","created_at":"2021-08-23T13:53:32.992000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"879362731638140940","reply_to_id":"879317328381214750","thread":null,"thread_id":null}
